datasets/cities_tz.csv
----------------------
Contains data from GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org/), licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
GeoNames provides the data "as is", without warranty or any representation of accuracy, timeliness
or completeness.

Source files, downloaded on 2026-09-26:
  https://download.geonames.org/export/dump/cities15000.zip
    sha256 9c1f26fa632212ad77e5b82b6d5df3b019a3c119e423efe59d7224a186f9c9f4
  https://download.geonames.org/export/dump/admin1CodesASCII.txt
    sha256 1da92a6323a5fec3176f3f743bf4cf4040fd56a876da55e46fbca23c863aa60a

Changes made to the GeoNames data:
  - Of the 19 columns of the GeoNames "geoname" table, only name, asciiname, country code,
    admin1 code, population and timezone are kept (renamed to name, asciiname, country_code,
    admin1_code, population, timezone).
  - A column admin1_name is added: the ASCII name of the first-level administrative division,
    joined from admin1CodesASCII.txt on "<country code>.<admin1 code>" (empty when GeoNames has no
    entry for that code).
  - Rows whose timezone is not a zone key of the tzdata package are dropped (no row was dropped
    on the download date: 34,149 rows kept).
  - Rows are sorted by ASCII name (case-insensitive), country code, admin1 code, descending
    population and name.
The file is produced by scripts/build_cities_tz.py.

datasets/tz_phrases.jsonl
-------------------------
The items with source "city_sample" contain city, region and country names taken from
cities_tz.csv, that is from GeoNames data (CC BY 4.0, see above).

Timezone data
-------------
Zone keys and the files zone.tab and iso3166.tab come from the IANA tz database
(https://www.iana.org/time-zones), which is in the public domain. They are read from the tzdata
Python package (version 2026.4, IANA release 2026d) when the datasets are built and checked; they
are not copied into this directory.
